WEBVTT FILE

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000


2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Arctic sea ice grows and shrinks with the seasons.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000


4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000


5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
NASA works with NSIDC to track sea ice,

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
identifying when it reaches its peak extent at the end of winter

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
and the annual minimum at the end of summer.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000


9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
This year, Arctic sea ice reached its maximum extent March 13, 2019.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Although it wasn’t a record, it continued a trend of declining maximums and minimums.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000


12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Sea ice plays an important role in regulating the planet’s climate, reflecting sunlight and heat back into space.

13
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000


14
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.091
NASA

